= World Wide Web — Technical =

Web architecture separates resource identity from any particular representation. A URI can identify a resource whose current representation is negotiated or generated dynamically. HTTP interactions operate on representations and metadata while preserving this abstraction.

== Modeling / implementation cautions ==
* World Wide Web ≠ Internet
* Web ≠ HTTP alone
* Web resource ≠ physical file necessarily

